::PC_U02_L06_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L06_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.EX.2
Question:
Which statement correctly interprets a logarithmic model?
{
=A. The logarithm asks for an exponent.#Correct. A logarithm identifies the exponent needed for a base to produce an argument.
~B. The argument may be 0 in every context.#A logarithm argument must be positive, so 0 is not allowed.
~C. The base of a logarithm can be 1.#A logarithm base must be positive and cannot equal 1.
~D. Logarithmic domains never have restrictions.#Logarithmic models require the argument to be positive.
}
